# PSR-5b — admin allowlist (documentation + ratchet)

## Why

PSR-5 inventory tagged two `apps/api/src` sites as
`tenant_path_allowlist_candidate`. Gate خروج PSR-5 requires every remaining
tenant-adjacent admin bypass to be a **small allowlist** with owner, reason,
and expiry — not an open-ended “we know about it” comment.

This wave **does not** remove or rewrite those call sites. It freezes them as
the only approved tenant-adjacent allowlist entries until a later reduction
wave.

## Allowlist (exact paths)

| ID | Path | Owner | Reason (summary) | Expiry |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `ALW-ID-FORCE-RLS` | `identity/prisma-identity.repository.ts` | identity | FORCE RLS on `user` / `mobileOtpChallenge`; pre-tenant login has no GUC | 2026-10-31 |

**Closed:** `ALW-FIN-TENANT-ROW` → PSR-5d (`findTenantFinanceWorkspaceRow` on registry port).

## Explicitly NOT on this allowlist

- `tenant/resolve-registered-tenant.ts` / `update-tenant-registry-row.ts` —
  **closed by PSR-5c** named port.
- `platform/*`, outbox, recon — control_plane / background_repair classes.
- Any new `getPrismaAdmin` under bookings/tours/HTTP routes — **forbidden**
  without a new allowlist PR.

## Ratchet

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-5b-admin-allowlist-smoke.mjs
```

Fails if:

- allowlist path loses `getPrismaAdmin(` (silent removal without inventory update);
- a new `tenant_path_allowlist_candidate` / `tenant_path_review` file appears
  outside the YAML set;
- expiry dates are missing or malformed.

## Non-goals

- Rewriting identity OTP/user to app-pool + RLS policies (separate design)
- Tenant registry port (PSR-5c)
- Harbor (PSR-6)
